WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.240
One of the problems people have with
electric cars is charging time.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.160
Yes, modern fast chargers can get
your car to 80% in about half an hour,

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.840
maybe even a little quicker
if you're lucky,

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.200
but that's a long time compared
to the three or four minutes

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.480
that it takes to fill up
with petrol or diesel.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.400
So when I first heard there
was a car company

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.160
building automated
battery swap stations,

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.320
where robots will switch out
your car battery

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.480
in just a few minutes,
while you stay in the car...

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.320
I assumed it'd be
a weird prototype,

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.080
some pie-in-the-sky technology
from a university

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:31.880
that would never become practical.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.520
But that is a
battery swap station,

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.240
right there,
open to the public,

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.680
so let's see if it works.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:43.040
- Nio has more than 2,100 stations
operational in China,

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:47.360
and the goal is to reach 2,300
by end of year.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.680
In Europe, we started around
two years ago,

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.640
and we have now 30
operational stations.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.880
In China, every day we have more than
40,000 battery swaps being performed,

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:00.840
one every two seconds.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.640
And we have had peaks during
holiday season,

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:05.440
more than 60,000 a day.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.880
We're not just piloting this,
it's already proven at scale.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.520
- As ever, this is not an advert,
they haven't paid me,

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:12.840
I reached out to them,

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.960
they have just let me borrow a car.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.720
[Car] "Please press the brake pedal."

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.120
"Nicely done!"

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.020
"Now you can tap to start parking
into the Power Swap station."

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.480
- You drive the car
in front of the station,

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.560
and once you park
in front of the station,

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.840
the car takes over.
And it's fully automatic.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.400
[Car] "We are parking now."

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.640
"Be aware of your surroundings."

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:37.040
"Do not open any door or
take over the steering wheel."

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:42.460
"You can press the brake panel
to control the speed."

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:49.600
- Nio users, if they want to access
the Power Swap network,

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.960
they need to choose
"Battery as a Service".

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.200
So that means they don't
own the battery,

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.320
they lease the battery,

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.920
and so they can get access to
the Power Swap station network.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.520
You can purchase
the battery and the car.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.840
Or you can purchase the car,

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.320
but choose access
to the swapping network.

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:08.760
You can also just subscribe to
both the car and the battery.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:12.920
- The idea is that you're not renting
or buying a specific battery,

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:17.040
but you're just paying for there always
being a fresh battery in your car.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.640
Charging is still a cheaper option,

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.480
but there are plenty of people
who'll pay a fee for convenience.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:24.180
[Car] "Preparing. Please wait."

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:29.000
- We can serve the same amount of
users comparable to a charging hub,

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.480
but we need only one third of the space

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:33.800
and we need one third of
the grid connection

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.520
because we can charge the
batteries at their low speed.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:39.480
We provide frequency balancing services.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:44.040
We charge the batteries
at specific points in time

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:49.000
where there is a need to get rid of
all that power and balance the grid.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.600
- The thing is, I've driven
electric cars on long trips before,

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.240
and charging wasn't
really a big problem:

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:57.760
it needs a little more planning
than using fossil fuels,

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.800
but turns out, I want to rest

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:02.440
at about the same interval
the car wants charging.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:05.680
Folks out there who can drive
eight hours in one go...

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.680
good luck, but I am not one of you.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:11.600
- The best way to charge a vehicle
is at home if you have a socket, right?

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.440
With EV becoming more affordable,

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:16.280
there are more people who want
to access an electric vehicle,

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:18.000
and don't have the opportunity

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.880
to have a socket close to
where they park their car.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:24.600
Shanghai, a city with more
than 20 million inhabitants,

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:29.360
people live in big apartments,
and so, on-street charging,

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.800
it's much less than in Europe.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:35.520
People don't have access to home charging
because it's a much more dense city.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.600
Power Swap offers a great opportunity

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:41.000
to just leave your home,
drive to the station,

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.000
swap your battery
and continue your trip.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.080
- And of course, there is the catch
that this battery swap station

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.360
only works for cars that
are built for it.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:49.960
You can get a Nio battery
swapped here,

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:52.560
but there's no other car on
the market that can use this.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.260
At least, not yet.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:04:00.440
- We have been signing strategic agreements
with big groups like Changan and Geely Group.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:04.280
We have gained the confidence
of also the other auto makers.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:08.160
There's a opportunity to
standardize this technology,

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.960
in China, but perhaps
also in Europe.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.160
We're going to invest
in Battery as a Service.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:16.600
And we're going to invest
in the Power Swap network.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:18.080
If you take the whole economics,

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:21.360
we do believe that this is better
than just selling a car.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.520
- Plenty of people,

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.680
electric vehicle enthusiasts,
stock brokers,

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:26.280
people who've bought Nio stock,

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.840
have a running analyses on whether the
company's financial model will work.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:32.360
Building these stations is
incredibly expensive,

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:35.760
and it's no secret that Nio is losing
a staggering amount of money right now,

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.080
but that's the way that
colossal startup companies

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.560
and finance work these days.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:42.680
They hope the initial outlay
will be worth it in the end.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:45.800
That strategy has paid off
for a lot of big corporations...

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.560
and not paid off for many more.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:49.400
I looked at a lot of those
financial analyses

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.080
while I was researching
and my conclusion is:

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:52.840
I don't know!

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:55.960
Predicting anything about electric vehicles
is almost impossible:

00:04:55.960 --> 00:05:00.360
it's an industry filled with both
radical inventions and broken promises.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:03.440
I'm just astonished that something
I thought was science fiction

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:07.440
does appear to be an actual
real-world option right now...

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:23.560
and that a robot just
swapped out my car battery.

